        "One shape expands for 5.5 seconds and contracts for 5.5 seconds, and that's the whole session. There are no holds to time and no number to track in your head. A voice can count the phases in your language, or you can switch it off.",
        "The pace is one slider, 3 to 10 seconds in half-second steps, and it drives the inhale and the exhale together so they stay equal. It's free for your first five qualifying sessions, a minute or longer, and part of Premium after that. The round count is always free, 1 to 200 or infinite, and the default is 27 rounds, which is 4:57.",
        "On Apple Watch the session runs on the wrist, and with heart rate tracking switched on the app keeps the first heart rate reading of the session and the last. The difference is on the completion screen and in your history. Coherent is the technique that gets asked about HRV, and it's the one where the app is most careful about that number.",
      ],
      aside: [
        "The default is 5.5 in and 5.5 out because that's where Lehrer and Gevirtz put the average resonance, and the slider runs 3 to 10 because resonance varies by person. It's the one phase setting I made adjustable. Box and 4-7-8 don't get a slider, because their ratio is the technique. Coherent's pace is a starting point, not a rule.",
        "I also rewrote the in-app description of coherent breathing to remove a causal claim about HRV. No single session can show that honestly, and the app's own audit script now blocks a release if a causal HRV claim comes back.",
      ],
